# Local design explorations / static preview mocks — not part of the app build.
design/

# Never let the private crate reach a public commit (scripts/with-private.sh).
#
# A whitelist of the files the stub is made of, not a list of the modules
# the private crate happens to have today: whatever goes private next is ignored
# here without anyone remembering to add it.
#
# Git cannot ignore modifications or deletions of these tracked stub files. The
# tracked pre-commit and pre-push hooks cover that half by refusing whenever the
# STUB marker is absent or Cargo.lock carries private dependencies.
crates/sealwire-private/*
!crates/sealwire-private/Cargo.toml
!crates/sealwire-private/STUB
!crates/sealwire-private/src/
crates/sealwire-private/src/*
!crates/sealwire-private/src/lib.rs
!crates/sealwire-private/frontend/
crates/sealwire-private/frontend/*
# Every public placeholder needs its own line here. Being tracked is not enough:
# ignore rules do not apply to tracked paths, so a missing exception still builds
# from a checkout — but tools that pack the repo through .gitignore (`railway up`)
# drop the file, and the broker image then fails on "Could not resolve".
!crates/sealwire-private/frontend/task-diff-react.js
!crates/sealwire-private/frontend/task-review-screen.js
!crates/sealwire-private/frontend/task-board-react.js
!crates/sealwire-private/frontend/task-ticket-screen.js
!crates/sealwire-private/frontend/composer-command-controller.js
